title: CobyGiftHunt_Intro
location: town
---

You think it would be nice to grab Coby a gift. After all, the time you spent together has been enjoyable. He's a little boring for a Marine, but his enthusiasm makes up for it. However, what would be the right gift for a person who'll probably say he likes anything? You ponder for a moment as you look over the various stalls and stores.
<<jump CobyGiftHunt_SelectStall>>
===

title: CobyGiftHunt_SelectStall
location: town
---

Three of them catch your eye as you look around. Coby isn't a flashy person, so you decide to go with something simple. With that in mind you decided to go to the
-> Bait and Tackle store. It looks a little run down, but maybe you can find him a new pole.
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_Baitandtackle>>
-> A cute accessory store. Most of the stuff in the window is a bit gaudy, but they have some headbands and glasses cases that Coby might like.
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_accessoryshop>>
-> A weird stall that seems to be selling some questionable souvenirs from past events. Some of it looks a little tacky, like an execution platform, but maybe Coby would appreciate the humor?
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_weirdstall>>
===

title: CobyGiftHunt_Baitandtackle
location: town
---

You decide to poke your head into the bait and tackle shop. The whole building unfortunately smells just like you thought it would, fish and whatever it is they're keeping the bait in. You look over the shelves. Different kinds of lures line the walls, sorted by sea and what they are supposed to catch, along with so many poles that it makes your head spin.
You bite your lip, pondering what to select as you study the selection of poles. You...
-> Select a beautifully crafted, well built pole that is colored in a gradient of pinks and purple. It looks more expensive than either of the poles you used on the ship, and Coby could use an upgrade.
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_perfectgift>>
-> Select a simple black rod. It doesn't look the best, but it will get the job done.
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_Okaygift>>
-> Select the least expensive option, a bamboo switch. You're not made of money, and Coby still might like it.
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_Badgift>>
===

title: CobyGiftHunt_Acessoryshop
location: town
---

A bell rings when you push open the door. The inside of the shop is very cozy and quaint, with little tables set up across the interior. Each one is laid out glamorously, with different theming. You go to look at one themed after aquatic animals. Three items catch your eye.
First, a blue headband with pink dolphins on it. It's cute and reminds you of the pod of dolphins you had seen while fishing. The dolphins match his hair, and you think he'd be cute in it.
Second, a red rhinestone crab pin. You can't help but laugh, thinking back to Coby's strange sentiment about crabs and buckets. Maybe he would enjoy it?
And finally, a glasses case with seashells printed on it. Coby is always wearing his on his head, so maybe this would be better?
You select one and take your purchase over to the counter, where the young man who runs the store greets you.
Storekeeper: That all for today?
You: Think so.
You purchased...
-> The blue headband with pink dolphins on it.
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_perfectgift>>
-> The red rhinestone crab pin.
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_perfectgift>>
-> The glasses case with seashells printed on it.
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_Okaygift>>
===

title: CobyGiftHunt_souvenirstall
location: town
---

You really don't know what to buy Coby, so you dart over to the little stall, which looks questionable at best. The items make you cringe, but you don't know what to buy someone who doesn't seem to want anything.
You grit your teeth, grab a gift off the stall and slam some berries down onto the counter. All of this seems tasteless, but it's better to have something then to come empty-handed, right?
You buy:
-> A Marine keychain
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_Okaygift>>
-> An “I fought at Marineford and all I got was this lousy t-shirt” shirt
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_Badgift>>
-> A “Rocky Port Oyster eating contest: We shuck em you suck em” shirt.
    <<jump CobyGiftHunt_Badgift>>
===

title: CobyGiftHunt_perfectgift
location: town
---

The shopkeeper smiles.
Shopkeeper: Whoever you are purchasing this for will love it.
<<jump CobyGiftHunt_Giftget>>
===

title: CobyGiftHunt_Okaygift
location: town
---
The shopkeeper nods as they ring you up.
Shopkeeper: Not a bad choice for a gift.
<<jump CobyGiftHunt_Giftget>>
===

title: CobyGiftHunt_Badgift
location: town
---
The shopkeeper looks uncertain but they ring you up.
Shopkeeper: You certainly have interesting taste.
<<jump CobyGiftHunt_Giftget>>
===

title: CobyGiftHunt_Giftget
location: town
---
You head out the store with your purchase in hand, feeling a little giddy. Coby is sure to like his gift. At least, you hope so.
===
